! Folds: a stroke nothing matched, read as another with something written around
! it. `dictionaries/folds.xfst` says how, and the base is in another dictionary.
! `scripts/check-hold.py` asks Plover the same questions.

! ---- a suffix key, and -T as "the"
!buffer
KAOEPT
!buffer
TAPGS
!buffer
RUPB
-G
! ---- onto a word of two strokes: the base extends the outline before it
!buffer
SEFRB
R-GTS
!buffer
PART
TK-PLTS
! ---- "and" before the base, and T- put back after H-
!buffer
SKPAD
!buffer
SKPHA
!buffer
SKPHAPBG
! ---- "and" needs its base to be a word, so a suffix still applies after it:
! SKPAOEP is "and keep" in user.json, then "the"
!buffer
SKPAOEPT
! ---- "is" before the base, S-, and "it's", ST-, where T- and the rest is no word
!buffer
STPHOU
!buffer
STPWAD
! ---- a real entry is never folded
!buffer
PWABGS
! ---- and "and" does not reach back over a word already written
!buffer
SEFRB
SKPAD
! ---- a word beside a `^` stroke: "a" before it, "of", "is" and "to" after it
!buffer
^TPOU
!buffer
^WOUFPB
!buffer
^THEUZ
!buffer
^OUPT
! ---- -T as "the" comes first, but ^PWAOBG writes nothing, so it is "back to"
!buffer
^PWAOBGT
